---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Software & Platform Engineer"
  description="Tyler Thomas is a software engineer focused on Python, backend systems, infrastructure, automation, and technical tooling."
>
  <main>
    <section class="hero site-width" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="eyebrow-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span> SOFTWARE / PLATFORM ENGINEERING</p>
        <h1 id="hero-title">Building software <span>and the systems behind it.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-description">
          I'm Tyler Thomas, a software engineer working across backend
          systems, API architecture, and infrastructure. Beyond building
          applications, I've helped establish the conventions, tooling,
          and operational practices that keep them maintainable.
        </p>
        <div class="hero-actions">
          <a class="action-primary" href="#work">Explore selected work <span aria-hidden="true">↘</span></a>
          <a class="action-text" href="https://github.com/tthomas63" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
          <a class="action-text" href="/notes/">
            Read engineering notes <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <aside class="focus-panel" aria-label="Engineering focus">
        <div class="focus-head"><span>FIELD NOTES / 001</span><span>TT—2026</span></div>
        <div class="focus-main">
          <p class="focus-kicker">AREAS OF FOCUS</p>
          <ol class="focus-list">
            <li><span>01</span><strong>Backend & API architecture</strong><small>Python, Django, resource design</small></li>
            <li><span>02</span><strong>Platform & reliability</strong><small>Deployments, infrastructure, recovery</small></li>
            <li><span>03</span><strong>Automation & tooling</strong><small>Integrations, data workflows, generation</small></li>
          </ol>
        </div>
        <p class="focus-foot">SELECTED PROJECTS, NOT AN EXHAUSTIVE RESUME.</p>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section class="work-section site-width" id="work" aria-labelledby="work-title">
      <div class="section-heading">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">01 / SELECTED WORK</p>
          <h2 id="work-title">Things I've built and worked through.</h2>
        </div>
        <p class="section-intro">A selection of independent projects and engineering problems, with the decisions behind them.</p>
      </div>

      <article class="featured-project" aria-labelledby="knit-title">
        <div class="featured-copy">
          <div class="featured-meta"><span>FEATURED PROJECT</span><span class="status-mark"><span aria-hidden="true"></span> IN DEVELOPMENT</span></div>
          <h3 id="knit-title">Django Knit<span class="project-slash">/</span></h3>
          <p class="featured-lead">Less repetitive glue between Django models, APIs, and frontend types.</p>
          <p class="featured-description">
            An independent tooling project exploring model-driven generation for Django REST Framework and TypeScript. The current work centers on explicit registration, predictable configuration, and maintainable output.
          </p>
          <a
            class="action-text featured-project-link"
            href="/projects/django-knit/"
          >
            Read project overview <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span>
          </a>
          <div class="tag-list" aria-label="Technologies used">
            <span>PYTHON</span><span>DJANGO</span><span>DRF</span><span>TYPESCRIPT</span>
          </div>
          <div class="featured-bottom"><span>INDEPENDENT DEVELOPMENT</span><span>MODEL-DRIVEN GENERATION</span></div>
        </div>
        <div class="diagram-panel" aria-label="Simplified diagram of Django Knit model configuration and generated outputs" role="img">
          <div class="diagram-head"><span>ARCHITECTURE / SIMPLIFIED</span><span>DK—001</span></div>
          <div class="diagram-content">
            <div class="diagram-node diagram-source">
              <span class="diagram-tag">INPUT</span>
              <strong>Django models</strong>
              <small>fields · relations · metadata</small>
            </div>
            <div class="diagram-connector" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
            <div class="diagram-node diagram-core">
              <span class="diagram-tag">CONFIGURATION</span>
              <strong>Knit registry</strong>
              <small>model registration + settings</small>
            </div>
            <div class="diagram-connector" aria-hidden="true"><span></span></div>
            <div class="diagram-output">
              <div class="diagram-node"><span class="diagram-tag">OUTPUT A</span><strong>DRF code</strong></div>
              <div class="diagram-node"><span class="diagram-tag">OUTPUT B</span><strong>TypeScript types</strong></div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="diagram-foot"><span>ONE CONFIGURATION</span><span>→</span><span>MULTIPLE OUTPUTS</span></div>
        </div>
      </article>

      <div class="more-work-heading"><p class="eyebrow">OTHER ENGINEERING WORK</p><span>02 — 04</span></div>
      <div class="work-list">
        <article class="work-entry">
          <div class="work-number">02</div>
          <div class="work-entry-content">
            <p class="work-type">INDEPENDENT / INFRASTRUCTURE</p>
            <h3>Linux server operations & automation</h3>
            <p>Containerized services, configuration management, logging, and practical troubleshooting tools for running dedicated servers.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="work-technologies">LINUX <span>·</span> DOCKER <span>·</span> AUTOMATION</div>
        </article>
        <article class="work-entry">
          <div class="work-number">03</div>
          <div class="work-entry-content">
            <p class="work-type">PROFESSIONAL / BACKEND</p>
            <h3>Legacy data import & migration workflows</h3>
            <p>Resource-specific Django/DRF import pipelines, domain validation, and transactional boundaries for moving legacy data into modern systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="work-technologies">PYTHON <span>·</span> DJANGO <span>·</span> DATA</div>
        </article>
        <article class="work-entry">
          <div class="work-number">04</div>
          <div class="work-entry-content">
            <p class="work-type">INDEPENDENT / ALGORITHMS</p>
            <h3>Navigation & procedural experiments</h3>
            <p>Explorations of graph-based navigation, waypoint systems, and procedural geometry in interactive environments.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="work-technologies">PATHFINDING <span>·</span> GEOMETRY <span>·</span> TOOLS</div>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="expertise-band" id="expertise" aria-labelledby="expertise-title">
      <div class="site-width expertise-inner">
        <div class="expertise-lead">
          <p class="eyebrow">02 / WHAT I WORK ON</p>
          <h2 id="expertise-title">The work behind the work.</h2>
        </div>
        
        <div class="expertise-columns">
          <div>
            <span>01</span>
            <h3>Backend & API architecture</h3>
            <p>
              Resource design, reusable API conventions,
              filtering strategies, data modeling,
              and integration workflows.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>02</span>
            <h3>Infrastructure & production engineering</h3>
            <p>
              Linux systems, deployments, database migrations,
              recovery planning, and operational troubleshooting.
            </p>
          </div>

          <div>
            <span>03</span>
            <h3>Automation & developer tooling</h3>
            <p>
              Reducing repetitive work through code generation,
              data pipelines, infrastructure automation,
              and practical developer tools.
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-section site-width" id="about" aria-labelledby="about-title">
      <div class="about-block">
        <p class="eyebrow">03 / ABOUT</p>
        <h2 id="about-title">Curiosity with a practical streak.</h2>
        <p>
          My experience spans backend applications, infrastructure,
          and data-intensive systems. Alongside implementation,
          I've developed API conventions, designed integration workflows,
          and worked through the operational consequences of software
          decisions in production.
        </p>
        <p>Outside conventional application development, I've spent years exploring navigation algorithms, procedural systems, and tooling built around real operational needs.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="contact-block" id="contact">
        <p class="eyebrow">04 / CONNECT</p>
        <h2>Let's talk engineering.</h2>
        <p>Interested in a technical discussion or my work? Start with the projects and background on my GitHub profile.</p>
        <a href="https://github.com/tthomas63" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">View GitHub profile <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
